2186045417 true] [17592186426856 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426856 1072 #uuid "973ba0d1-71e0-5bd1-b707-8f3f23076709" 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426856 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 2 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ 12{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=16 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second  equation yields\n\n$$\n12{x}_{2}+2(2)=16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+4(1)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+1+2=5.\n$$" 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426857 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426855 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426857 1069 "q-112247" 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426857 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426857 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426857 1072 #uuid "ad22bfb4-da83-594b-af3c-ca1a05478310" 13194139534592 17592186045417 true] [17592186426857 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-4)+(-3)=-7.$" 13194139534592 17